A running or ready pod isn't in sync yet. It first copies the records written while it was away. Only once it reaches the leader's log end offset does the leader add it back to the ISR. That gap is exactly why Strimzi waits before restarting the next broker.

With no ack, the producer retries to the new leader, which doesn't have it, so it's written once. When the old broker rejoins, it uses the leader epoch history to truncate the records the new leader never had. The result is exactly one copy, with no loss and no duplicate.

